REVISION (2026-11-24, second session)
WHAT CHANGED (dashboard only; lib/model.ts, main.ts, model formula, board rows and farm plans untouched)
- Top movers strip on the board (#/): the 5 board rows (all pre-token) with the largest positive 7d TVL
  change, ties by rank, from the same data.js. Each card shows rank, name, 7d change, implied value and a
  value bar, and links to #/protocol/<slug>. Hidden whenever a search, category, chain or scope filter is
  active (same condition as the filter chips); a sort-only URL is not a filter and keeps it.
  Current movers: #42 Shift DeFi +4448.47%, #182 Monolith Market +162.86%, #112 NUVA +160.80%,
  #143 Theo Network thBill +94.01%, #104 August Digital +77.98%.
- app.js dedupe: shared sgn() (signed %) used by pct() and the detail growth text; mult(n, d) replaces
  x() and four inline "n/a or n.toFixed(d)+'×'" copies; bar(), tag(), nChains(), plink(), hero(),
  card(), foot() and rows() replace repeated markup, map/join, plural and link code; one input listener
  loop for search/category/chain; live view reuses catOf().
- Dead code removed: ageOf() (never called), the one-use `below` variable, a header comment that said
  "four views" while listing five.
- app.css: one shared rule for the uppercase label style (thead th, .card h2, .kv th, .movers h2);
  .pager a:hover folded into .btn:hover; .fbar reuses .bar's track/fill rules.
  Added a global [hidden] { display: none !important }. This also fixes an old bug: .chips
  { display: flex } overrode the hidden attribute, so an empty chip bar was always drawn on the board.
- Dropped the tooltip titles on the board's WATCHLIST/EARLY tags (the detail view never had them).

